{%- comment -%}
  snippets/portal-account-href.liquid — where the header's account link should go
  (spec task 19.3, design §25.2, §25.3).

  Requirements 22.1, 22.2, 22.3.

  ── WHY THIS EXISTS AT ALL ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  §25.3's coexistence table lists exactly one change to a live layout file: "one
  flag-gated link change to point the account icon at the portal (Branch B)". The
  account icon is in `sections/header.liquid`, not `layout/theme.liquid` as that row
  says — the design predates the header being split into its own section. The change
  is made where the link actually is.

  ── WHY A SNIPPET AND NOT SIX LINES OF LIQUID IN THE HEADER ───────────────────
  §25.2 requires the flag to be evaluated in ONE server-side place. `{% render %}`
  is scope-isolated, so a snippet cannot hand a boolean back to its caller — but its
  OUTPUT can be captured, which is enough:

      {%- capture portal_href -%}{% render 'portal-account-href' %}{%- endcapture -%}

  So the gate condition is written once, here and in `portal-chrome`, rather than
  copied into the header where it could drift from the one the pages use. A drifted
  copy is the specific failure this avoids: an account icon pointing at the portal
  while the portal pages themselves still render `page.content`.

  ── OUTPUT CONTRACT ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Emits `/pages/my-athoor` when the portal is on AND a customer is signed in.
  Emits NOTHING otherwise — including for an anonymous visitor with the flag on,
  because sending a stranger to a page that will only invite them to sign in is
  worse than sending them to the sign-in route the theme already uses.

  The caller keeps its own `else` branches, so with the flag off the rendered href is
  byte-identical to today's. That is the property the tests assert in both
  directions.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- liquid
  assign portal_on = false
  if settings.portal_enabled
    assign portal_on = true
  elsif settings.portal_allowlist != blank and customer
    assign needle = ',' | append: customer.id | append: ','
    assign hay = ',' | append: settings.portal_allowlist | append: ','
    assign hay = hay | replace: ' ', ''
    if hay contains needle
      assign portal_on = true
    endif
  endif

  if portal_on and customer
    echo '/pages/my-athoor'
  endif
-%}
